# Frontend Rules

Stack: Vue 3 `<script setup>` + TS, Vite, Pinia, Vue Router, shadcn-vue (Reka UI), Tailwind CSS **v4**, Axios.

## UI priority

1. Prefer existing shadcn-vue components under `src/components/ui/`
2. Install via CLI when missing: `pnpm dlx shadcn-vue@latest add <name>`
3. Custom components only when shadcn cannot meet the need
4. Project MCP `.mcp.json` exposes shadcn-vue MCP—use it when component docs/patterns are needed

## Styling

- Tailwind v4 only (`@import "tailwindcss"`, CSS-first theme)
- Prefer semantic theme tokens (`bg-background`, `text-muted-foreground`, etc.) over raw colors
- No Tailwind v3-only patterns

## Auto-import

unplugin-auto-import / vue-components: Vue, Vue Router, Pinia, local components/composables are auto-imported. Still **manually import VueUse** and non-auto modules (`@/api`, `@/lib`, icons).

## Composables / Pinia

- Destructure composable returns (VueUse style)
- For Pinia state refs use `storeToRefs`; do not destructure store state without it

## API layers

| Layer | Location | Pattern |
|-------|----------|---------|
| API defs | `src/api/*.ts` | `request<T>({ method, url, data })` |
| Stores/composables | JS layer | call api + `.catch` |
| Views | `views/**` | `useRequest` for loading/error UX |

Do not call raw axios from views when `request` / `useRequest` exist.

## Forms & icons

- Forms: vee-validate + zod when validating
- Icons: `lucide-vue-next`

## Port

Dev web: **3000** (`pnpm run dev:web`). Do not start it unless the user asks.
